# Build output is committed for GitHub Pages — never reformat it.
docs/
node_modules/
play-store/
package-lock.json

# Content data files use hand-tuned alignment that Prettier would destroy
# (column-aligned word tables, curriculum rows). Reformatting them would
# produce an enormous, unreviewable diff for no readability gain.
src/data/

# Data tables that happen to live outside src/data/. Same rule, same reason:
# each of these is a hand-maintained lookup table where the column alignment
# IS the readability, and Prettier rewrites every row onto its own line.
#   audio.js         grapheme → MP3 file, and grapheme → TTS spelling. Two
#                    tables of ~150 entries; flattened they run to 400 lines
#                    and you can no longer see at a glance which sounds have
#                    a recording and which fall back to speech.
#   phonemeColors.js sound type → label, colour and diacritic mark.
#   letterSounds.js  phoneme type → label, short label, colour, bg, order.
src/modules/audio.js
src/modules/phonemeColors.js
src/modes/letterSounds.js

# The app shell. Prettier re-indents all 1,456 lines (everything inside
# <html> shifts two spaces) and explodes every element with more than one
# attribute — ~1,550 changed lines for no readability gain on a file that is
# already consistently formatted, just to a tighter convention. It is also
# the one hand-written file whose exact markup is what ships.
index.html
